From 51c85c2e512f6124f6fe0abeb2702a8e113a452f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:34:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(deburr): picked and excluded edges, minimum edge
 angle, hole filter

A 3D Deburr now breaks only the picked edge chains when its source is a
selection, leaves out the chains in `exclude_edges`, skips a convex
crease that bends less than `min_edge_angle_deg`, and skips the rims of
recognized round holes inside a diameter range.

- motion: `finishing3d::deburr_edges` and the `deburr_filter` module.
  `deburr` keeps its behaviour with the filters at rest.
- app: the new `OpParams::Deburr` fields with their sanity door, seed,
  stamp digest and project-file keys (absent at rest, so an old file
  reads and saves unchanged). `operation/deburr_picks.rs` resolves the
  picked and the excluded chains. The MCP pick door takes edge chains
  only for a Deburr.
- ui: the Deburr Geometry tab has the minimum edge angle, the hole
  filter and the excluded-edge list.

A pick that names no rim or convex crease is refused by name. A pick
that is not an edge chain is refused by name.

Fixes #1888

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
