From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:35:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(deburr): read a directed hole's wall span by its
 travel sign

After the merge of main (#2601), a `CrossHole` wall point at travel `d`
stands at `origin - dir * d`. The hole filter read the span with the
other sign and matched only the mouth ring. The far rim of a cross hole
stayed in the ride. The span now uses the negated travel scalars, and a
cross-hole test pins the two rims.

Refs #1888

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
